    "chunkId": "85813ad241a2b45087d057967a494040420ebca8350b3e0513294730286dd074",
    "text": "# Install Docker Engine\n\nThis guide explains how to install Docker Engine.\n\n> **Note:** Docker Engine requires a 64-bit kernel.\n\n## Prerequisites\n\nBefore installing, review the supported platforms.\n\n| Platform | Supported |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ubuntu | Yes |\n| Debian | Yes |\n| CentOS | No |\n\n## Install using the convenience script\n\nRun the following commands:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSL https://get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh\nsudo sh get-docker.sh\n```\n\n## Post-installation steps\n\nComplete these steps after installing:\n\n- Create the docker group\n- Add your user to the group\n- Log out and back in\n\n\n## See also\n\nSee the release notes for details.",
